sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (agreed with Nick, 2026-11-07): a task VM is disposable; its slot identity stays with the Gateway.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: tasks:cancel
  %% kind: tasks.cancel
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit the release<br/>revoke the claim's keys
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Pi token and model key of the claim are revoked; approved work is pushed first, as today
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-tasks-cancel
  SW->>H: Delete the VM<br/>and its seed clone
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one host exec: `incus delete --force` and the seed clone; a few seconds
  %%> - no Node, DNS, Metrics or hub peer change: the identity stays
  %%> - beside it, the claim's model key is revoked at the model router; the Pi token goes with the VM
  SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>identity free
  Note over GW: Free the slot identity<br/>target under 10 s
